    "instruction": "Improve the whole ordinary program using the function contracts and measured examples. Check whether the information passed across interfaces suffices for the requested result. You may change ANY function/interface/state, add/remove helpers or replace the whole program. Choose the simplest useful refactoring; preserving correct code is allowed.",
    "current_program": "def investigate(context, acquire):\n    values = context[\"values\"]\n    n = len(values)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    contrib = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        x = values[i]\n        p = -2 * x + 0 * x * x + 0 * x * x * x\n        g = 0\n        if i > 0:\n            g = 0 * x * values[i - 1]\n        contrib.append(p + g)\n    for passnum in range(2):\n        acc = 0\n        newlist = []\n        for v in contrib:\n            acc = acc + v\n            newlist.append(acc)\n        contrib = newlist\n    return contrib[-1]\n",
